<title>ISRAEL: PALESTINIAN GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>PALESTINIAN GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>PALESTINIAN GOVERNMENT LIST (970124)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 6 Jan 97 - PLO leader Yasser Arafat won a landslide	 *</p>
<p> *		victory in the first direct elections in	 *</p>
<p> *		Palestinian history in the West Bank, including*</p>
<p> *		Arab East Jerusalem, and the Gaza Strip in     *</p>
<p> *		January 1996. The Palestinian cabinet	    *</p>
<p> *		(Authority) is in charge of parts of the West  *</p>
<p> *		Bank and Gaza Strip in line with a PLO-Israel  *</p>
<p> *		interim peace deal. The fate of Palestinian    *</p>
<p> *		territories would be determined in final-status*</p>
<p> *		talks that have yet to resume under Israel's   *</p>
<p> *		new government.					  *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>  President......................................Yasser ARAFAT</p>
<p>(Also Minister of the Interior)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>General Secretary of the</p>
<p>	Palestinian Presidency.................Tayeb ABDEL-RAHIM</p>
<p>General Secretary of the</p>
<p>	Palestinian Authority.................Ahmed ABDEL-RAHMAN</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS (Sworn in by the Palestinian Legislative Council</p>
<p>		 on June 27, 1996)</p>
<p>  Agriculture...............................Abdel-Jawwad SALEH</p>
<p>  Civil Affairs................................Jamil al-TARIFI</p>
<p>  Culture &amp; Information......................Yasser ABED RABBO</p>
<p>  Education.........................................Yasser AMR</p>
<p>  Finance.........................Mohammed Zuhdi al-NASHASHIBI</p>
<p>  Health.....................................Riyadh al-ZAANOUN</p>
<p>  Higher Education...............................Hanan ASHRAWI</p>
<p>  Housing...................................Abdel-Rahman HAMAD</p>
<p>  Industry................................Bashir al-BARGHOUTHI</p>
<p>  Interior.......................................See President</p>
<p>  Justice....................................Freih ABU MEDDEIN</p>
<p>  Labour.........................................Samir GHOSHEH</p>
<p>  Local Government.................................Saeb EREKAT</p>
<p>  Planning &amp; International Cooperation............Nabil SHAATH</p>
<p>  Public Works..................................Azzam AL-AHMAD</p>
<p>  Social services............................Intissar al-WAZIR</p>
<p>  Supplies..................................Abdel-Aziz SHAHEEN</p>
<p>  Telecommunications..........................Imad al-FALLOUJI</p>
<p>  Tourism..........................................Elias FREIJ</p>
<p>  Trade &amp; Economy...............................Maher al-MASRI</p>
<p>  Transport....................................Ali al-QAWASMEH</p>
<p>  Waqf &amp; Islamic Affairs........................Hassan TAHBOUB</p>
<p>  Youth &amp; Sports...................................Talal SIDER</p>
